<title>USA: Calif tax assessors sue IBM, state tax authority.</title>
<headline>Calif tax assessors sue IBM, state tax authority.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>County assessors throughout California filed a complaint in Superior Court Friday naming International Business Machines Corp as a party to a lawsuit over taxation of computer software.</p>
<p>The action, filed against the California State Board of Equalization, the state's taxing authority, challenges that authority's effort to exempt computer programs from property taxes, court papers said.</p>
<p>The lawsuit by the assessors says this effort is invalid and contrary to the state tax code.</p>
<p>IBM was not available for comment.</p>
</text>
